<title>UK: Ashbourne surges on 177p/shr cash offer.</title>
<headline>Ashbourne surges on 177p/shr cash offer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British nursing homes company Ashbourne Plc leapt on Wednesday after U.S. backed Exceler Health Care Group announced an agreed takeover at 177p per share, valuing Ashbourne at 95 million stg.</p>
<p>The shares put on 14p to reach a record high of 175p.  </p>
<p>Exceler, owned by the Sun Health Care Group Plc, already owns 29.2 percent of the British group.</p>
<p>Commenting on the offer, Chet Bradeen, managing director of Exceler, said, &quot;the acquisition of Ashbourne will establish the enlarged group as one of the UK's most significant players in the nursing home market.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
